  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "The product of a certain whole number and four more than that number is 140. Find the number.\n\nIntroduce a pronumeral, write down a quadratic equation and solve it.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$10$",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the whole number.\n$$\\begin{align*}n(n+4)&=140\\\\n^2+4n-140&=0\\\\(n+14)(n-10)&=0\\\\n+14&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad n-10=0\\\\n&=-14\\quad\\text{or}\\quad n=10\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n$ is a whole number, reject $-14$. The number is $10$.\n\nCheck: $10(10+4)=140$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
